  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor level (FULL) and load knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1">Author H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs — inject IKeyVaultClient, IArmClient, ISecretCatalogManifestReader, IIdempotencyService, ICosmosRunStore.</step>
    <step order="2">Load canonical secret-catalog manifest via ISecretCatalogManifestReader (Phase H artifact).</step>
    <step order="3">For each secret entry: check exists; if fresh-populate, write with canonical name per §7.9; if upgrade mode + secret exists, NO-OP unless explicit H4-rotate variant.</step>
    <step order="4">BINDING pre-check: assert Dataverse-ClientSecret + BFF-API-ClientSecret exist BEFORE any deletion op; fail deploy with "BindingPreCheckViolation" on any deletion attempt.</step>
    <step order="5">PATCH App Service keyVaultReferenceIdentity to UAMI resource ID on BOTH prod + staging slots (T1); post-condition ARM read verifies.</step>
    <step order="6">Interim T5 mitigation: grant KV Secrets User role to BOTH slot System-Assigned MI principals (fetched from ARM); structurally superseded post-Phase-C.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify BFF /health returns 200 resolving Dataverse:ClientSecret KV ref (NFR-05); fail deploy if not.</step>
    <step order="8">Author unit tests: (a) fresh populate happy, (b) upgrade-mode rotation-safe no-op, (c) H4-rotate variant explicit rotation, (d) T1 verify success, (e) T1 verify fail (mismatch), (f) T5 both-slot grant, (g) BINDING-do-not-delete guard, (h) idempotency.</step>
    <step order="9">Register in L2 Program.cs DI.</step>
    <step order="10">Run dotnet build + dotnet test; verify green + zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change task 047 status from 🔲 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviations in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If keyVaultReferenceIdentity PATCH silently fails (T1 verification fails despite ARM PATCH returning 200), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — root cause is likely UAMI not existing yet (Phase C uami.bicep gap) OR Bicep app-service.bicep refactor not merged; do NOT retry-loop.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Phase H canonical secret-catalog manifest (task 080) has not landed, DEFER this task — do NOT invent a local manifest.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any existing Dataverse-ClientSecret or BFF-API-ClientSecret is missing on the target KV at H4 start (indicates prior drift), STOP and escalate — BINDING pre-check violation.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: seeding logic in scripts (per Phase G/H); no existing L2 handler. Canonical secret-catalog manifest is Phase H deliverable (task 080).</existing>
    <extension>No — this handler owns two silent-fail traps (T1 + T5 interim) and a BINDING pre-check; wrapping it around scripts alone can't provide DAG advancement + Cosmos state writes + rotation-safe upgrade semantics.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without H4 as a handler owning T1 verification, App Service boots but every KV-ref setting is null (T1 silent failure — see design.md §4B T1). Without T5 interim mitigation, slot-swap produces 503 window until Phase C UAMI lands. Without BINDING pre-check, an unintended manifest change could delete Dataverse-ClientSecret and break OBO across the entire fleet (severity: fleet-wide outage).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell + az CLI for ARM PATCH</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.Tests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a fresh customer (sprk_provisionedon == null) and a canonical secret-catalog manifest, when HandleAsync runs, then all manifest secrets are populated to KV at canonical names per §7.9 (env-agnostic, one canonical casing) with vault name from Bicep parameter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T1 (spec.md FR-33): ARM read confirms App Service keyVaultReferenceIdentity == UAMI resource ID on BOTH prod and staging slots; deploy fails with trap-T1 code if not.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T5 interim (spec.md FR-33 T5): BOTH slot System-Assigned MI principals have KV Secrets User role granted (interim mitigation); pre-Phase-C-UAMI-complete only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Upgrade mode rotation-safe: given a live secret exists on KV, when H4 runs in upgrade mode without H4-rotate variant, then it is a NO-OP (no overwrite).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Upgrade mode rotation-explicit: given H4-rotate variant, when H4 runs, then the specific secret is rotated (audit-logged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative BINDING guard: given a manifest change that would delete Dataverse-ClientSecret or BFF-API-ClientSecret, when H4 runs, then it fails with "BindingPreCheckViolation" and does NOT proceed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-05 fail-fast: after secret population, BFF /health returns 200 resolving Dataverse:ClientSecret KV ref; H4 fails deploy otherwise.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency: two invocations for the same customerId + secretsVer — second call is a no-op (kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer} match).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cleartext-secret leak check: Cosmos parameters + interStepState contain NO string matching known secret patterns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI; dotnet build + dotnet test exit 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-07 + FR-33 (T1 + T5 interim) + FR-34 (upgrade rotation-safe) + FR-35 canonical naming + MUST rule (do-not-delete) + NFR-05; design.md §4.1 H4 + §4B T1/T5 + §7.9. Depends on Phase H task 080 (canonical secret-catalog manifest).

